    "index.does.title": "Real tasks, done for you.<br>Not just answers.",
    "index.does.lead": "Cedar searches the web, reads your files, runs the numbers and writes the result: a report, a spreadsheet, a map, a chart. For bigger tasks you see the plan before the work starts, and the sources when it's done.",
    "index.does.schedule.title": "Works on its own, even while you sleep",
    "index.does.schedule.body": "Turn any conversation into an agent that runs every morning at 7, or when something happens: a price drops, an email arrives, a meeting is about to start. It tells your desktop or phone when it's done.",
    "index.does.schedule.alt": "Cedar for Mac scheduling a daily sailing weather report for 10:00 AM",
    "index.does.actions.title": "Learns your actions, and uses the computer privately",
    "index.does.actions.body": "When there's no tool for a job, show Cedar how: record your screen while you do it once, and it writes down the steps and follows them next time. For what only exists behind windows, it works a desktop with the mouse and keyboard: one in a container, or your own, where it asks before it acts.",
