    "index.cmp.eyebrow": "Compared",
    "index.cmp.title": "Cedar, OpenClaw, OpenBot, Meta Muse,<br>OpenAI Dots, Claude Duet and Claude Managed Agents.",
    "index.cmp.lead": "Seven ways to have an agent do tasks for you. <a href=\"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw\">OpenClaw</a> lives in your chat apps and acts on your computer. <a href=\"https://openbot.run/\">OpenBot</a> runs a team of agents such as Codex and Claude Code on your computer. <a href=\"https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/\">Meta Muse</a> runs in Meta’s cloud. <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-dots/\">OpenAI Dots</a> is an always-on agent on its own computer in OpenAI’s cloud. <a href=\"https://claude.com/product/claude-duet\">Claude Duet</a> is Anthropic’s, a proactive agent on its own computer in Anthropic’s cloud. <a href=\"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/self-hosted\">Self-hosted Claude Managed Agents</a> is Anthropic’s agent platform for companies, run on their own servers while the model stays with Anthropic or a cloud provider. Cedar runs at home, on a Mac, a Windows PC or a Linux box, and keeps every task in its own sealed box.",
